IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`
IMPORT `cat-regulations-2012`
IMPORT `part-1-preliminary`
IMPORT `part-2-div-2-microchipping`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA), compilation 00-l0-01, currency start 25 Sep 2025 (mrdoc_48898).
-- Part 2 Division 3 -- Sterilisation: ss 18-21. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01.
-- (Division 2 is imported only for its helper `every item of _ is among _`.)

§ `Section 18 -- Cats to be sterilised`

-- s 18(2): "A cat is exempt from sterilisation if any of the following apply in respect of the
-- cat — (a) a certificate given by a veterinarian stating that to sterilise the cat may
-- adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat applies in respect of the cat; (b) the cat
-- is owned, for the purpose of breeding, by an approved cat breeder; (c) the cat belongs to a
-- class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation."
-- s 18(3): "A certificate referred to in subsection (2)(a) cannot apply in respect of a cat
-- that is under 6 months of age." FORK-13 reading A, as for s 14(3).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(2)(a), (3) (FORK-13 reading A)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(2)(a) -- a health certificate applies to` c `on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation health certificate`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST cert THEN
            "a certificate given by a veterinarian" ... cert's `given by`'s `is a veterinarian`
        ... "stating that to sterilise the cat may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat"
            ... cert's `states that the procedure may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat`
        ... `the day number of` (cert's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` t
        ... "(3) cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6 months of age"
            ... c `has reached 6 months of age on` t

-- (b) is judged by the owner whose position is in question: the encoding knows an owner's
-- approval only from that owner's own record (REF-01). See ENCODING-NOTES.md.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`, o IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(2) --` c `is exempt from sterilisation on` t `, owned by` o IF
        "(a)" ... `s 18(2)(a) -- a health certificate applies to` c `on` t
    ..  "(b) owned, for the purpose of breeding, by an approved cat breeder"
            ... c's `is owned for the purpose of breeding`
            ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t
            ... o's `is an approved cat breeder`
    ..  "(c)" ... `no regulation -- belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` c

-- s 18(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is
-- sterilised by a veterinarian, unless the cat is exempt from sterilisation.
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000." In operation from 1 November 2013 (s 2(c)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) --` c `is sterilised by a veterinarian on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN
            `s 3(1) --` c `is sterilised on` t
        ... "by a veterinarian" ... s's `performed by`'s `is a veterinarian`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is sterilised applies to` o `for` c `on` t IF
        "The owner" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t
    ... "of a cat that has reached 6 months of age" ... c `has reached 6 months of age on` t
    ... "unless the cat is exempt from sterilisation" ... NOT `s 18(2) --` c `is exempt from sterilisation on` t `, owned by` o
    ... `the day number of` (`the date` 2013 11 1) AT MOST `the day number of` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) --` o `contravenes the subsection for` c `on` t IF
        `s 18(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is sterilised applies to` o `for` c `on` t
    ... "must ensure that the cat is sterilised by a veterinarian" ... NOT `s 18(1) --` c `is sterilised by a veterinarian on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(b)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 18(1) -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 18"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a subsection, but not at the foot of the section`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 18(1)"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 19 -- Identifying as sterilised a cat that is not sterilised`

-- s 19: "A person must not identify a cat as sterilised in the manner prescribed if it is not
-- sterilised. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." The manner: Cat Regulations r 18.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 19; Cat Regulations 2012 r 18
GIVEN m IS A `Means of identification`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19 -- identifying by` m c `as sterilised on` t `contravenes the section` IF
        "identify a cat as sterilised in the manner prescribed" ... `r 18 -- is the manner prescribed` m
    ... "if it is not sterilised" ... NOT `s 3(1) --` c `is sterilised on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 19; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 19 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 19"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 19"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 20 -- Notice of sterilisation to be given to microchip database company`

-- s 20: "A veterinarian who sterilises a microchipped cat must, within 7 days after sterilising
-- the cat, give notice in writing in the form, if any, prescribed of the sterilisation of the
-- cat to the microchip database company for that cat. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- No form is prescribed (REF-37). "Microchipped" is judged on the day of sterilising.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 -- the duty to notify applies to the sterilisation of` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN
            "A veterinarian" ... s's `performed by`'s `is a veterinarian`
        ... "who sterilises" ... `s 3(1) --` c `is sterilised on` (s's `performed on`)
        ... "a microchipped cat" ... `s 3(1) --` c `is microchipped on` (s's `performed on`)
        ... "to the microchip database company for that cat" ... `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20; Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 20 -- the last day for notice of the sterilisation of` c `given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date` 1970 1 1
    WHEN JUST s THEN `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` (s's `performed on`) `given the holidays` holidays

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, notice IS A MAYBE `Notice`, t IS A `Calendar date`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 -- the veterinarian contravenes the section for` c `, the notice being` notice `, on` t `given the holidays` holidays IF
        `s 20 -- the duty to notify applies to the sterilisation of` c
    ... `the day number of` (`s 20 -- the last day for notice of the sterilisation of` c `given the holidays` holidays) LESS THAN `the day number of` t
    ... NOT `in time`
    WHERE
        `in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER notice
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST n THEN
                    n's `in writing`
                AND n's `given to` EQUALS `the name of the microchip database company for` c
                AND `the cat's sterilisation status` `is an item among` (n's `items`)
                AND `the day number of` (n's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` (`s 20 -- the last day for notice of the sterilisation of` c `given the holidays` holidays)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 20 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 20"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 20"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 21 -- Certificate of sterilisation to be given`

-- s 21: "A veterinarian who sterilises a cat must give a certificate of sterilisation to the
-- owner of the cat. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." No time is fixed. When failure to give it
-- becomes a contravention is Interpretation Act s 63 ("with all convenient speed"), which the
-- reference register does not name and which is not encoded: the encoding says only whether
-- the duty arose and whether, by day t, it has been done.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 21
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 -- the duty to give a certificate applies to the sterilisation of` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN
            "A veterinarian" ... s's `performed by`'s `is a veterinarian`
        ... "who sterilises a cat" ... `s 3(1) --` c `is sterilised on` (s's `performed on`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 21
GIVEN t IS A `Calendar date`, c IS A `Cat`, `given to` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 -- by` t `the certificate for` c `has been given to an owner, it being given to` `given to` IF
    CONSIDER `given to`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n THEN n `is an owner of` c `on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 21; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 21 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 21"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 21"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Interpretation Act s 71 -- which duties continue`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(1)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 20 is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing within a period or before a time`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2) (FORK-12 reading A)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 18(1) is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing with no period or time specified`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 21 is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing with no period or time specified`
